{"author":"rebar-bridge[bot]","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","data":{"compacted_at":1795153994616967002,"compiled_state":{"alias":"transhuman-wounded-pangolin","assignee":null,"author":"Rebar Bot Nava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","authorship":{"signed":3,"unsigned":0},"authorship_ledger":[{"content_hash":"d8338cec74ecf6ce0e2c5f964ac1bbe2e6c3f60ca6bc7fc17defa20a16c8f12e","event_uuid":"19135029-f291-40f9-a144-ff8dcbc07727","position":{"commit_sha":"10914c5ad547974e94a123383af762b78572ecc7","position":"1795153939525534001-19135029-f291-40f9-a144-ff8dcbc07727"},"signature":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","signer_pubkey":"ssh-ed25519 AAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAIMQNvvCya66a6YyDlxwkxjjJPN3uaFI+QD3OjyC8e1UF rebar-mac-492a5c71 joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com 20261119"},{"content_hash":"dd649cc8636f3ca6089fdaeba7aaa6c678dc5eccfe98d1cba0c8560cf387c722","event_uuid":"e11ca302-6982-4c70-bf2f-627b7eb57c8b","position":{"commit_sha":"74c727e341c314ba94ee27e054384423ab3fd52a","position":"1795153963352178001-e11ca302-6982-4c70-bf2f-627b7eb57c8b"},"signature":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","signer_pubkey":"ssh-ed25519 AAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAIMQNvvCya66a6YyDlxwkxjjJPN3uaFI+QD3OjyC8e1UF rebar-mac-492a5c71 joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com 20261119"},{"content_hash":"6c3805b5d9a8d4d2672af67cfb947db7dbd7fb80a900114da5165c774fea0fdb","event_uuid":"ee5fb760-1f0b-4652-803f-8df82b8c5c69","position":{"commit_sha":"6af7ff2d8a9a1b2951958fd0541addc2585dc630","position":"1795153994616967001-ee5fb760-1f0b-4652-803f-8df82b8c5c69"},"signature":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","signer_pubkey":"ssh-ed25519 AAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAIMQNvvCya66a6YyDlxwkxjjJPN3uaFI+QD3OjyC8e1UF rebar-mac-492a5c71 joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com 20261119"}],"bridge_alerts":[],"bridge_project":null,"claim_harness":null,"claim_remote_session":null,"claimed_session":null,"comments":[],"created_at":1795153939525534001,"creation_channel":"cli","deps":[{"link_uuid":"e11ca302-6982-4c70-bf2f-627b7eb57c8b","relation":"discovered_from","target_id":"8aa0-2120-5ef3-4750"}],"description":"## Context / Problem\nDiscovered while triaging breezy-hogged-mastiff, which owns `.github/windows-sweep-deselect/unclassified.args`. These 55 entries move to `.github/windows-sweep-deselect/posix-shell-stubs.args`, which this bug owns.\n\nThese tests install fake `git`/`uv`/`acli`/`scc` executables as shebang scripts on `PATH`, run `bash`/`sh`/`make`, or symlink a tool into a stub directory. On the Windows runner the stubs never run (the count and args files they write are missing: `test_makefile_worktree.py`, `test_repo_isolation_guard.py`), the stubbed timeouts never fire (`test_snapshot_git_watchdog_d33f.py`, `test_snapshot_submodules_watchdog_c605.py`, `test_delta_tree_timeout_b0e0.py`, `test_store_write_git_timeout_c2ba.py`: DID NOT RAISE), and `bash` resolves to the WSL launcher, which prints a UTF-16 \"no installed distributions\" message (`test_git_floor_gate_tree_skew.py`, `test_predates_gate_guard_parity.py`).\n\nEvidence: Windows runs on throwaway branch `tmp/w05-remeasure` with origin/main `717c50f8b33` code plus a selection-only workflow change: run 44665461131 (the 242 `unclassified.args` entries; 48 passed, 194 failed or errored) and run 44681457334 (the 194, xdist, JUnit XML with full tracebacks). Both 2026-11-19 PST.\n\nModules:\n- `tests/interfaces/test_metrics_polyglot.py` (4)\n- `tests/scripts/test_check_readme_quickstart.py` (1)\n- `tests/scripts/test_jira_pressure_test_preflight.py` (6)\n- `tests/scripts/test_mutation_sandbox.py` (2)\n- `tests/unit/metrics/test_scc_loc.py` (1)\n- `tests/unit/reconciler/test_acli_preflight_missing_binary.py` (2)\n- `tests/unit/test_check_criteria_vocabulary.py` (1)\n- `tests/unit/test_check_shellcheck.py` (3)\n- `tests/unit/test_child_oracle_fail_open.py` (4)\n- `tests/unit/test_ci_workflow_parity.py` (1)\n- `tests/unit/test_delta_tree_timeout_b0e0.py` (2)\n- `tests/unit/test_gerrit_verify_triage_comment.py` (3)\n- `tests/unit/test_git_floor_gate_tree_skew.py` (1)\n- `tests/unit/test_makefile_worktree.py` (6)\n- `tests/unit/test_predates_gate_guard_parity.py` (1)\n- `tests/unit/test_repo_isolation_guard.py` (4)\n- `tests/unit/test_serena_grep_reminder_hook.py` (1)\n- `tests/unit/test_session_shims.py` (1)\n- `tests/unit/test_snapshot_git_watchdog_d33f.py` (4)\n- `tests/unit/test_snapshot_submodules_watchdog_c605.py` (4)\n- `tests/unit/test_store_write_git_timeout_c2ba.py` (1)\n- `tests/unit/test_worktree_python_pin.py` (2)\n\n## Approach\nPer module: replace shebang stubs with a portable stub (a Python script launched through `sys.executable`, or a `.cmd` shim on Windows), or skip tests whose subject is a POSIX shell recipe. Remove each line from `posix-shell-stubs.args` as it passes.\n\n## Scope\nTest or product code for the listed modules, plus `.github/windows-sweep-deselect/posix-shell-stubs.args` (remove each fixed line; delete the file and its `@` reference in `.github/workflows/test.yml` once empty).\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n- [ ] Every line removed from `posix-shell-stubs.args` names a test that passed in a `sweep (windows)` run on main after the fix (run id recorded in a comment).\n- [ ] `posix-shell-stubs.args` is empty and deleted with its reference in `.github/workflows/test.yml`, or each remaining line names a test recorded on this ticket as intentionally unsupported on Windows with the reason.\n","env_id":"492a5c71-6cda-48a6-8134-02ff6a672739","file_impact":[{"path":".github/windows-sweep-deselect/posix-shell-stubs.args","reason":"remove each line as its test is fixed"}],"file_impact_scope":"paths","keyring":[],"managed_refs":[],"no_file_impact_reason":"","parent_id":null,"parent_status_uuid":"","plan_review_phase":"planning","preconditions_summary":{"status":"pre-manifest"},"priority":3,"releases":[],"repos":[],"reverts":[],"status":"open","tags":["windows","portability"],"ticket_id":"e062-1686-1a27-41a4","ticket_type":"bug","title":"Windows sweep: 55 tests drive POSIX shell scripts, make recipes or shebang stub executables","verify_commands":[]},"source_event_uuids":["19135029-f291-40f9-a144-ff8dcbc07727","e11ca302-6982-4c70-bf2f-627b7eb57c8b","ee5fb760-1f0b-4652-803f-8df82b8c5c69"]},"env_id":"","event_type":"SNAPSHOT","timestamp":1795153994616967002,"uuid":"4070b4d5-52ea-4377-a850-c8db87863084"}
